<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6706" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">captīvĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		captivus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the condition of</i> captivus (post-Aug.; cf.
			Madvig. Cic. Cornel. Fragm. ap. Orell. V. 2, p. 71). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of living beings, <i>captivity</i>, <i>bondage</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep.
				85, 27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 12, 51</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 25</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">11, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. H. 5, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 3, 5,
				2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 3</span></i>. 3;
			4, 5, 12; 11, 3, 7; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">11, 14, 11.—Also of animals,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 37, 56, § 134</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Flor. 1, 18,
			28</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Collect.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nisi coetu alienigenarum, velut captivitas,
					inferatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 11, 23</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b> Of
			inanim. things, <i>a taking</i>, <i>capture</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 16, 16</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				H. 3, 83</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Africae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					2, 6, 8</span></i>
			.—Also in plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					3, 70</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			(Acc. to capio. II. A. 2. a.) Oculorum, <i>blindness</i>, <i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 104, 36</span></i>
			Elm.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
